INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_entry` (`ID`, `Kind`, `Zone`, `SortOrder`, `Faction`, `RequiredState`, `Title`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(36100, 0, 361, 0, 0, 0, 'Felwood', 'Felwood was once the northern reach of Ashenvale, a serene forest tended by the night elves beneath Mount Hyjal. In the Third War the Burning Legion made it a weapon. To weaken the kaldorei before the demons marched on Hyjal, the dreadlord Tichondrius used the Skull of Gul''dan to poison the land, and nothing was spared: the trees blackened, the beasts went mad, ancients were twisted and the waters turned foul. Illidan Stormrage later took the skull and destroyed Tichondrius, yet the taint remained, and so did the demons. The Shadow Council plots with the Legion from Jaedenar, Jadefire satyrs defile the old elven ruins, and infernals still stalk the craters where they fell. The Deadwood furbolgs have been driven mad, while in the north the Timbermaw alone of their race stayed pure. From the Emerald Sanctuary, druids of the Emerald Circle labor to heal what they can. The Horde keeps Bloodvenom Post on the western cliffs, and the night elves hold Talonbranch Glade in the north.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Felwood (once part of northern Ashenvale; Archimonde had it corrupted before Hyjal; Tichondrius and the Skull of Gul''dan; Illidan took the skull and defeated Tichondrius; Shadow Council in Jaedenar; Bloodvenom Post only Horde post, Talonbranch the Alliance one); quest 4261 description (Skull of Gul''dan, infernals, all fell to the corruption); quest 8460 description (Timbermaw the only furbolg tribe to escape the corruption); quest 5155, 4421 descriptions; npc_text 3874 (Eridan); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Bloodvenom_Post (high cliffs overlooking Darkshore)'),
(36101, 1, 361, 1, 0, 0, 'Morlos''Aran', 'At the southern edge of Felwood, near the Ashenvale border, stand the ruins of Morlos''Aran. Before the Sundering it was a great night elf settlement, kin to Ameth''Aran in Darkshore and Ordil''Aran in Ashenvale, and its broken stones now serve only to recall a golden age lost long ago. The corruption has not spared it. Felpaw wolves, Angerclaw bears and Ironbeak owls roam among the ruins, and the great wolf Death Howl hunts these southern woods. Here the night elf druid Arathandris Silversky of the Emerald Circle keeps her post, seeking anyone willing to help her reclaim Felwood.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Morlos''Aran (southern edge, pre-Sundering settlement, sister ruins, memorial to a golden age); zone_areas.py: Arathandris Silversky 9528, Felpaw Wolf, Angerclaw Bear, Ironbeak Owl, Death Howl 14339 in area 2478; npc_text 2844, 2845 (Arathandris gossip; she speaks Darnassian)'),
(36102, 1, 361, 2, 0, 0, 'Emerald Sanctuary', 'Hidden among the trees of southern Felwood, the Emerald Sanctuary is the camp of the Emerald Circle, a largely independent branch of the Cenarion Circle sworn to undo the corruption of this land. Its druids are friendly to all who come in peace. The tauren Greta Mosshoof directs the war on the Shadow Council, Eridan Bluewind strikes at the Jadefire satyrs, and Taronn Redfeather searches for even a single pure source of water in the forest. Jessir Moonbow, come from Darnassus with her wolf Della, waits here for friends long overdue from Jaedenar. Nearby on the road stands Grazle, a Timbermaw furbolg seeking allies for his tribe.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Emerald_Circle (largely autonomous branch of the Cenarion Circle, stationed at the Emerald Sanctuary); zone_areas.py area 2479: Eridan 9116, Greta 10922, Taronn 10921, Kelek 10920, Ivy and Tenell Leafrunner, Jessir 11019, Della 11024, Gorrim 22931, Grazle 11554; quest 5128 completion text (Emerald Circle is friendly to all); quest 5156 reward text (Taronn''s failed search for pure water); npc_text 3864 (Jessir); quest 8460 log (Grazle near the Emerald Sanctuary); creature_template 11024 (type beast, display 1030 DireWolf); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Della (wolf)'),
(36103, 1, 361, 3, 0, 0, 'Deadwood Village', 'Southwest of the Emerald Sanctuary, toward the Ashenvale border, lies Deadwood Village, the chief camp of the Deadwood furbolgs. Like most of their race they fell to the fel, which poisons their minds and turns them against all others. Deadwood warriors, pathfinders and gardeners fill its huts, and the Timbermaw ask their allies to drive this camp back first. The village answers to Overlord Ror, a great befouled furbolg, and the savage Ragepaw prowls nearby. Ror is blamed for the loss of at least one hero: an orc warrior who roamed Felwood fighting the Shadow Council went after him at a druid''s request, and neither was heard from again.', 'zone_areas.py area 1761: Deadwood Warrior, Gardener, Pathfinder, Overlord Ror 9464, Ragepaw 14342; quest 8460 description (first Deadwood tribe to my west); quest 8461 description (effects of the fel pollute their minds); quest 6162 description (Ror near the Ashenvale border, husband and druid never heard from again); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Deadwood_tribe (Deadwood Village their capital)'),
(36104, 1, 361, 4, 0, 0, 'Ruins of Constellas', 'Northwest of the Emerald Sanctuary stand the Ruins of Constellas, once one of the many night elf settlements near Mount Hyjal. Its moonwell, long a symbol of renewal for the kaldorei, has been fouled with fel energy, and the Jadefire satyrs who hold the ruins use its waters to bring forth more of their kind. Their leader here is the cruel Xavathras, who spreads the sickness to every creature he can. Felsworn, shadowstalkers and rogues haunt the broken walls, cursed oozes seep among the stones, and the Forsaken of Bloodvenom Post have taken an interest in the well''s water.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Ruins_of_Constellas (one of many night elf settlements near Hyjal, moonwell corrupted with fel); quest 4421 description (northwest of the Sanctuary, Xavathras spreads the disease); quest 4906 description (cultivate a corrupted moonwell for Xavaric); quest 4505 description (moonwell once a symbol of renewal, now used to bring forth more satyrs); zone_areas.py area 2481: Xavathras 9454, Jadefire Felsworn, Shadowstalker, Rogue, Cursed Ooze'),
(36105, 1, 361, 5, 0, 0, 'Jadefire Glen', 'In the south of Felwood, west of the Emerald Sanctuary, a wooded hollow called Jadefire Glen is one of the homes of the Jadefire satyrs, the tribe that has made the corruption of Felwood its feast. Satyrs and felsworn crowd the glade, and among them, seldom seen, walks Alshirr Banebreath. Even here a corrupted whipper root clings to life, sickly and slime coated, in desperate need of care if it is ever to be made whole.', 'zone_areas.py area 2480: 33 Jadefire Satyr, 20 Jadefire Felsworn, Alshirr Banebreath 14340 (rare), Corrupted Whipper Root 164888; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Jadefire_satyr (Jadefire Glen one of their homes; Alshirr a member); quest 4906 description (satyrs feed upon the corruption of native creatures); quest 4117 completion text; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Alshirr_Banebreath (rare satyr at Jadefire Glen)'),
(36106, 1, 361, 6, 0, 0, 'Bloodvenom Post', 'Bloodvenom Post is the Horde''s only foothold in Felwood, a small camp on the high cliffs above Darkshore, close by the poisoned Bloodvenom River. Braves stand guard, a wind rider master links it to the rest of Kalimdor, and merchants trade goods and weapons. Those who linger have their own purposes. The Forsaken Winna Hazzard experiments with corrupted moonwell water, Trull Failbane looks beyond Timbermaw to Winterspring and the night elf secrets its wildkin are said to guard, and the orc widow Dreka''Sur waits for vengeance on the furbolg who took her husband.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Bloodvenom_Post (pre-Cataclysm: small Horde outpost near the river, high cliffs overlooking Darkshore); zone_areas.py area 1997: Bloodvenom Post Brave, Brakkar wind rider master, Bale, Altsoba Ragetotem, Winna 9996, Trull 10306, Dreka''Sur 9620; quests 4505, 4506, 4521, 6162'),
(36107, 1, 361, 7, 0, 0, 'Bloodvenom Falls', 'Through the heart of Felwood runs the Bloodvenom River, its water thick with the forest''s poison, and at Bloodvenom Falls it spills into fouled pools where tainted oozes breed. The largest of them, a hulking mass called the Ongar, lurks below the falls. The riverbanks belong to the Shadow Council: its warlocks, darkweavers and enforcers walk them openly, and the tunnels of their fortress run beneath.', 'zone_areas.py areas 1764, 1765: Tainted Ooze, Vile Ooze, The Ongar 14345 (rare ooze), Jaedenar Warlock, Darkweaver, Enforcer; posarea: Shadow Lord Fel''dan and Ulathek (Shadow Hold, underground) stand over grid areas 1764 and 1765; darkshore.json Cliffspring River entry (Thundris traces the taint east to Felwood)'),
(36108, 1, 361, 8, 0, 0, 'Jaedenar', 'West of the road in central Felwood lies Jaedenar, raised on ancient night elf ruins and druidic barrow dens and now named in worship of Kil''jaeden. It is the seat of the Shadow Council on Azeroth, the cult that claims credit for much of the suffering of the orcish people, and here it plots with the Burning Legion. Cultists, adepts and guardians patrol the ruins with their hounds, warlocks and darkweavers practice their arts, and legionnaires stand among them. At its center a moonwell still holds water, corrupt like all else here. Below lies Shadow Hold, the cult''s fortress, warded by spells bound to burning braziers.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Jaedenar (built on night elf ruins and two barrow dens, named for Kil''jaeden, seat of the Shadow Council); quest 5155 description (path to the west, the Council plots with the Legion); npc_text 3864 (Jessir: claim responsibility for much of the orcish race''s suffering); quest 5157 description (Moon Well in the center of Jaedenar, Shadow Hold, braziers); zone_areas.py area 1763: Jaedenar Cultist, Adept, Guardian, Hound, Warlock, Darkweaver, Legionnaire'),
(36109, 1, 361, 9, 0, 0, 'Shadow Hold', 'Beneath Jaedenar lies Shadow Hold, the Shadow Council''s chief fortress, and a single path winds down through it with no other way in. Four braziers of protection, called Pain, Malice, Hatred and Suffering, keep its depths hidden from scrying eyes. The cult keeps prisoners caged and torturers at hand. The warlock Ulathek has his own quarters here and boasts that he holds counsel with dreadlords, and in his chamber the dreadlord Lord Banehollow keeps court with his attendant Ur''dan. In the deepest halls waits one called Shadow Lord Fel''dan, attended by the succubi Moora and Salia.', 'quest 5242 description (no other ways in, straight path down, Fel''dan the mortal in power below, two succubus servants); quest 5165 description and gameobjects 176158-176161 (Braziers of Pain, Malice, Hatred, Suffering); npc_text 7038 (Ulathek holds counsel with dreadlords); quest 7624 (Ulathek''s quarters in the Shadow Hold); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Lord_Banehollow (dreadlord, Ur''dan his attendant); DB creature.areaId 1770: Banehollow, Ur''dan, Ulathek, Salia, Arko''narin, Remains of Trey Lightforge; cage gameobject 176306; WMOAreaTable.dbc rows 31165-31185 (WMO 3093 -> 1770); vmaps 001_*.vmtile: Barrowdens_C.wmo uid 167780; floor ray casts of spawn positions'),
(36110, 1, 361, 10, 0, 0, 'Shrine of the Deceiver', 'Among the ruins of Jaedenar, one of the old druidic barrow dens has been given over to the Shadow Council and renamed the Shrine of the Deceiver, after Kil''jaeden, the lord of the Burning Legion whom the cult reveres. Where druids once slept, cultists, adepts and guardians keep its chambers with their hounds, and it is a dangerous place for the unprepared. The Emerald Circle sends would-be allies into these corrupted dens to thin the cult''s ranks before trusting them with greater tasks.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Shrine_of_the_Deceiver (corrupted barrow den named for Kil''jaeden, filled with Shadow Council warlocks, dangerous for the unprepared); DB creature.areaId 1771: Jaedenar Adept, Cultist, Guardian near 4770,-550; quest 5155 description (enter the depths of one of the corrupted Barrow Dens they inhabit); WMOAreaTable.dbc rows 31152-31164 (WMO 1290 -> 1771); vmaps: Corruptbarrowdensoneroom.wmo uid 169047; floor ray casts of spawn positions'),
(36111, 1, 361, 11, 0, 0, 'Shatter Scar Vale', 'North of Bloodvenom Falls, east of the road, the land is pocked with craters where infernals were hurled down during the last great war. The craters still smolder and still hold the corrupt, fetid water that gathered in them years ago, and entropic beasts and horrors roam among them. The infernals themselves remain, brainless but destructive, and the mightiest of them is Immolatus. The vale has an unlikely resident too: the gnome warlock Niby the Almighty, who has made camp here with his imp near the burned-out remains of an infernal named Kroshius.', 'quest 5156 description and reward (north, east of the road, infernals called down in the last great war, entropic elementals, corrupt water still there); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Shatter_Scar_Vale (north of Bloodvenom Falls, still smoldering craters); zone_areas.py area 1766: Entropic Beast, Entropic Horror, Infernal Sentry, Immolatus 7137 (rare elite), Niby 14469, Impsy 14470, Kroshius 14467; quest 7603 (Kroshius lies in a heap in the vale)'),
(36112, 1, 361, 12, 0, 0, 'Jadefire Run', 'In the north of Felwood the Jadefire satyrs keep their second great encampment at Jadefire Run, ruled by the cruel Xavaric. Hellcallers and tricksters crowd the camp, feeding on the corruption of the forest''s native creatures, and the beasts that roam its edges, Felpaw scavengers, Angerclaw maulers and Ironbeak hunters, carry that corruption plainly. Even the plants are sick: corrupted windblossoms, a night dragon and a whipper root struggle for life among the satyrs.', 'quest 4906 description (second encampment to the north, Xavaric, hellcallers, betrayers, tricksters); quest 939 and 4441 descriptions (flute carved from an ancient protector, spirit bound and tortured); zone_areas.py area 2618: Xavaric 10648, Jadefire Trickster, Hellcaller; item 11668 Flute of Xavaric drops from Xavaric at 100 percent; zone_areas.py area 2618: Felpaw Scavenger, Angerclaw Mauler, Ironbeak Hunter; Corrupted Windblossom 174601, 174602, Night Dragon 174608, Whipper Root 174606'),
(36113, 1, 361, 13, 0, 0, 'Irontree Woods', 'Irontree Woods spreads across northern Felwood, once a peaceful glade and now as corrupted as the rest of the forest. Crazed treants, the irontree stompers and wanderers, roam alongside warpwood elementals, toxic horrors and maddened grizzlies and owls. At the southern edge of the woods lie ruins where many corrupted treants once dwelt. Older presences are said to linger too. Vartrus, Stoma and Hastat, ancients who protected this forest and whose bodies were destroyed when the Legion marched upon Hyjal, are said to keep watch in spirit still, sharing their secrets only with those who prove worthy.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Irontree_Woods (once a peaceful glade, crazed treants, ancients Hastat, Stoma, Vartrus); zone_areas.py area 1767: Irontree Stomper, Irontree Wanderer, Warpwood Moss Flayer, Warpwood Shredder, Toxic Horror, Angerclaw Grizzly, Ironbeak Screecher, Vartrus 14524, Stoma 14525, Hastat 14526; quest 4442 reward text (ruins in southern Irontree Woods, corrupted treants, spirits); quest 7633 reward text (ancients, physical forms destroyed when Archimonde marched upon Hyjal, spirits intact)'),
(36114, 1, 361, 14, 0, 0, 'Irontree Cavern', 'A cavern beneath the Irontree Woods shelters warpwood elementals, moss flayers and shredders that the druids of the Emerald Circle believe are now beyond any hope of cleansing. Their sap, which the druids call blood amber, is studied by Arathandris Silversky and Maybess Riverbreeze in the hope of saving other life in Felwood, and killing these lost creatures is how both druids judge whether a stranger truly serves the Cenarion Circle. Deep in the cave lurks Dessecus, a powerful elemental.', 'quest 4101/4102 description and reward (Irontree Caverns to the north, Warpwood elementals beyond hope of cleansing, blood amber); DB creature.areaId 1768: Dessecus 7104 (rare elite elemental), Warpwood Moss Flayer, Warpwood Shredder; WMOAreaTable.dbc rows 31186-31195 (WMO 1552 -> 1768); vmaps: Md_Mushroomcave05.wmo uid 184143; floor ray casts of spawn positions'),
(36115, 1, 361, 15, 0, 0, 'Talonbranch Glade', 'Talonbranch Glade is a small night elf post in northern Felwood, south of Timbermaw Hold, built around a moonwell. It is the Alliance''s only refuge in the corrupted forest. A hippogryph master links it to the other roosts of Kalimdor, and merchants offer weapons and supplies. Teachers keep the old disciplines alive here: Kaerbrus instructs hunters, Nalesette Wildbringer trains their pets, and the night elf druid Golhine the Hooded counsels that peace can be found anywhere, even within cold stone walls, by looking inward for balance. Golhine warns young druids that one day the Emerald Dream will call them to sleep for years and walk among the purest of forms.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Talonbranch_Glade (small night elven post with a moonwell, south of Timbermaw Hold, Golhine); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Felwood (Talonbranch the Alliance equivalent of Bloodvenom Post); zone_areas.py area 1998: Mishellena 12578 hippogryph master, Malygen, Mylini Frostmoon, Kaerbrus 5501, Nalesette Wildbringer 543, Golhine 9465; npc_text 4783, 4784 (Golhine); creature_template_model 9465 display 10738 (night elf male); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Golhine_the_Hooded; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Talonbranch_Glade (pre-Cataclysm: small post with a moonwell)'),
(36116, 1, 361, 16, 0, 0, 'Felpaw Village', 'In the far north of Felwood, just southwest of the gates of Timbermaw Hold, lies Felpaw Village, a camp of the Deadwood furbolgs. Den watchers, avengers and shamans guard it under Chieftain Bloodmaw, and corruption hangs heavy over its huts. Nafien, the Timbermaw guard at the nearby gate, grieves that his tribe must fight its own kin here. In the camp a cauldron bubbles with a rotting, repulsive sludge, and runners of the Winterfall tribe come down from Winterspring to carry shipments back to their village. The ritual totems its furbolgs carry give off a palpable despair.', 'zone_areas.py area 1762: Deadwood Den Watcher, Avenger, Shaman, Chieftain Bloodmaw 9462, Winterfall Runner 10916, Deadwood Cauldron 176091; quest 8461 description (camp directly southwest of Nafien, corruption permeates it, saddened to fight brethren); quest 5084 reward text (cauldron), 5087 description (runners carry shipments to Winterfall Village); quest 8470 description (ritual totem, palpable sense of despair); item 20741 drops from Den Watcher, Avenger, Shaman'),
(36117, 1, 361, 17, 0, 0, 'Timbermaw Hold', 'Timbermaw Hold is the home of the Timbermaw furbolgs, cut into the mountains of northern Felwood, and its tunnels are the road from Felwood to Moonglade and Winterspring. While the forest outside rotted, the Timbermaw weathered the storm here, the only furbolg tribe to escape the corruption. They pay for it with suspicion. So many outsiders kill furbolgs on sight that the tribe trusts almost no one, and strangers who have not proven themselves are attacked within the hold. Nafien guards the Felwood gate and Salfa the Winterspring one. Inside, the gruff trader Gorn One Eye, Kernda, who studies the totems of the corrupted tribes, and Meilosh, who holds mooncloth sacred, deal with the few they trust.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Timbermaw_Hold (home of the tribe, weathered the storm, paths to Moonglade and Winterspring, residents); quest 8460 description (only tribe to escape the corruption, trust very few); quest 8462 reward (strangers met with open hostility in the Hold); quest 8465 description (Salfa at the Winterspring entrance); quest 6032 (mooncloth sacred); DB creature.areaId 1769: Gorn One Eye 11555, Meilosh 11557, Kernda 11558; posarea Nafien 15395 in 1769; WMOAreaTable.dbc rows 31196-31239, 46734 (WMO 2256 -> 1769)'),
(36118, 2, 361, 1, 0, 0, 'Greta Mosshoof', 'Greta Mosshoof is a tauren druid of the Emerald Circle at the Emerald Sanctuary who leads the Circle''s fight against the Shadow Council. She welcomes all who would protect this once mighty forest, but warns them not to be swayed by the power that soaks the land, for it will corrupt them as it corrupted Felwood. Her trust is earned in battle against the cult, and she explains why plainly: it weakens the foe, and it builds respect between allies. She prefers knowledge to haste, spying on Shadow Hold by scrying before any attack. She counts the shaman Islen Waterseer an old friend, and her prayers go to the Earthmother.', 'npc_text 3807 (Greta gossip); quest 5155 description and completion text; quests 5157, 5158, 5165 texts (scrying, Islen an old friend, Earthmother); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Greta_Mosshoof (tauren druid)'),
(36119, 2, 361, 2, 0, 0, 'Eridan Bluewind', 'Eridan Bluewind is a night elf druid of the Emerald Circle who works from the Emerald Sanctuary. She notes the bitter truth that Felwood is named for the very thing that corrupted it, yet she still believes the corruption can one day be erased. Her chief enemies are the Jadefire satyrs, who spread their disease to every creature they meet, and she means to defend a land that was once her people''s. Seekers of Un''Goro Crater''s mysteries find their way to her as well.', 'npc_text 3874 (Eridan gossip); quest 4421 description and reward; quests 939 reward, 4441, 4442; quests 4005, 4084 (Un''Goro quests she starts, QuestSortID 490); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Eridan_Bluewind (night elf druid, female, Emerald Sanctuary before 4.0.3a)'),
(36120, 2, 361, 3, 0, 0, 'Lord Banehollow', 'Lord Banehollow is a dreadlord of the Burning Legion, one of the nathrezim, and he keeps a chamber of his own within Shadow Hold, the Shadow Council''s fortress beneath Jaedenar. His attendant Ur''dan waits close at hand, and the warlocks, darkweavers and legionnaires of the Hold keep the halls around him. To any mortal who reaches his chamber uninvited he is a deadly foe, a demon lord who meets intrusion with his dark magic rather than with words.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Lord_Banehollow (dreadlord, leader of Jaedenar, rival Hel''nurath, Ulathek a spy, Ur''dan attendant); quests 7623 (Shadowy Potions, reward text on patience), 7624 (Ulathek plots with Hel''nurath on Xoroth, heart), 7625 (Xoroth domain of Hel''nurath, stardust from Ur''dan at a price); FactionTemplate.dbc 1434 (hostile to all players); gameobject 175724 Sargeras and the Betrayal, page_text 1776 (the Nathrezim, also known as dreadlords); quest 13251 description (dreadlords known racially as the Nathrezim)'),
(36121, 2, 361, 4, 0, 0, 'Niby the Almighty', 'Niby the Almighty is a gnome warlock camped in Shatter Scar Vale with his imp Impsy, and he commands every visitor to bow in his presence, certain they can feel the power he holds over them. His ambitions run to infernals. Nearby lie the burned out remains of one called Kroshius, and to a fellow warlock who rekindles that corpse, destroys it and brings back the infernal core from its burning remains, Niby will teach the secret of summoning an infernal servant. Impsy, for his part, privately considers his master daft.', 'creature_text 14469 (bow down, kicked out of Stormwind, infernal destroyer, chicken, death by chicken); creature_text 14470 (Impsy mocking); npc_text 7001 (Niby gossip); quests 7601, 7602, 7603 (infernal core of Kroshius, teach summoning an infernal servant); smart_scripts 1446900 (Call Infernal Destroyer after 7603); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Niby_the_Almighty (gnome warlock)'),
(36122, 2, 361, 5, 0, 0, 'Arko''narin', 'Arko''narin is a night elf held captive by the Shadow Council, locked in a cage within Shadow Hold beneath Jaedenar. Cold and hungry, she begs anyone who comes near to help her escape, certain that one of her captors carries the key. She did not come alone. Her friend Trey was taken with her, and she fears he is already dead, unable to bear the thought of what the cultists may have done to him. She still believes there is time to save herself, though she is sure that before long they will sacrifice her to whatever demons they worship.', 'npc_text 3865, 4113 (Arko''narin gossip); quest 5203 description and reward (Lightforge, superiors, Darnassus, no time for the druids); quest 5204 completion text (Knight of the Silver Hand); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Arko''narin; creature_template_model 11020/11141 (human male displays); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Trey_Lightforge (human male paladin)'),
(36123, 2, 361, 6, 1, 0, 'Arei', 'Arei is the spirit of one of Felwood''s ancient protectors, bound to the land''s suffering even after death. Arei remembers a peaceful and serene forest before the Legion came with its infernals, destruction and chaos, and the Skull of Gul''dan, which ensured that nothing was spared: all fell to the corruption. Trapped by it still, the spirit cannot rest, and asks only to be led through the cursed forest toward home, where it may finally be at peace. Once free, Arei bids its guide seek out the druid Kayneth Stillwind in Forest Song, in eastern Ashenvale.', 'quest 4261 description, log and reward (Kayneth: every kind deed helps); creature_text 9598 lines 0-7; npc_text 2726, 2809; smart_scripts 9598 (escort), event_scripts 3839 (Arei summoned at 5998.7,-1208, posarea 1767); ashenvale.json Kayneth notes (4261 left to Felwood)'),
(36124, 2, 361, 7, 0, 0, 'Grazle', 'Grazle is a Timbermaw furbolg who stands on the road near the Emerald Sanctuary, far from his tribe''s hold, seeking friends among outsiders. He calls the Timbermaw the last of the furbolg race to remain uncorrupted, and it pains him that few believe such a thing possible. Most strangers kill furbolgs on sight, and in anger his brethren now attack anyone who comes near. Grazle still hopes that peace can be made with those who show by their deeds that they come as allies. To any who fight the corrupted Deadwood, he is a patient friend, and he makes sure their deeds are known among his kind.', 'npc_text 4393 (Grazle gossip); quest 8460 description and reward; quest 8466 completion and reward text; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Grazle (male)'),
(36125, 2, 361, 8, 0, 0, 'Gorn One Eye', 'Gorn One Eye keeps a trader''s stall deep within Timbermaw Hold, dealing with the few outsiders his tribe has come to trust. He is warier than most of his kin. To a stranger who has won over only a handful of the Timbermaw he has little to say: he sees them, they may be on their way, and it will take more than the trust of a few to prove anything to him. Yet in time it is Gorn who brings the tribe''s gravest task to those who have earned its trust.', 'npc_text 4399 (Gorn gossip); quest 8481 description and reward (summon the demon at High Chief Winterfall''s cave, Essence of Xandivious, chance at survival); quests 8484, 8485 (offering of peace to Magni and Thrall, who had tried to make contact); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Gorn_One_Eye (general goods vendor)'),
(36126, 2, 361, 9, 2, 0, 'Dreka''Sur', 'Dreka''Sur is an orc of Bloodvenom Post whose husband traveled Felwood for the honor of their clan, battling the Shadow Council and the forest''s other abominations. He cheated death many times. His last letter told her that a druid had asked his help against a great befouled furbolg called Overlord Ror, and after that neither warrior nor druid was heard from again. Left a widow and unable to rest, Dreka''Sur wants Ror''s clawed hand, caring nothing whether the beast is corrupt or merely savage from living in so dismal a forest, so long as it pays for its crimes against her family.', 'quest 6162 description, completion and reward text; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Dreka''Sur (female orc, Bloodvenom Post)'),
(36127, 2, 361, 10, 2, 0, 'Winna Hazzard', 'Winna Hazzard is a Forsaken at Bloodvenom Post who admits that some call her exceptionally cruel, though she insists she only wants the Horde to gain every advantage over the Alliance, in any way possible. Her newest interest is the corrupted moonwell at the Ruins of Constellas, south of the post, once a symbol of renewal for the night elves and now a font that brings forth more satyrs. She has an idea for its water, and wants a sample brought to her for the sake of her little feline friend, the kitten that keeps her company.', 'quests 4505, 4506 texts; creature_text 9996 (pours the water on the cat, perfect); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Winna_Hazzard (Forsaken); creature 10658 Winna''s Kitten beside her'),
(36128, 3, 361, 1, 0, 0, 'The Shadow Council in Jaedenar', 'Greta Mosshoof of the Emerald Circle will not trust anyone against the Shadow Council until they have proven themselves its enemy, for the cult is responsible for many evils in Felwood and far beyond it. Its seat is Jaedenar, along a path to the west, where it plots with the Burning Legion. So her would-be allies first descend into one of the corrupted barrow dens there to slay its hounds, guards, adepts and cultists. She knows that shedding blood as proof of honor disgusts some, but it serves two ends: it weakens the foe, and it builds a respect between allies that will make them stronger in the times to come.', 'quests 5155, 5157, 5158, 5159, 5165, 5242 descriptions, completion and reward texts'),
(36129, 3, 361, 2, 0, 0, 'The Prisoner of Shadow Hold', 'Jessir Moonbow came from Darnassus to meet two friends at the Emerald Circle''s camp near the Ashenvale border, but they are days late. They had gone into Jaedenar to learn whether the Shadow Council, which claims credit for much of the orcish race''s suffering, is regaining its power. Among the cult''s servants, meanwhile, some carry a strange key, small and red and made of some kind of bone, heavy in the hand yet very fragile. Why a member of the Shadow Council would carry such a thing is a mystery, and somewhere in Jaedenar there must be something it unlocks.', 'npc_text 3864 (Jessir), 3865, 4113 (Arko''narin); quests 5202, 5203, 5204, 5385 texts; smart_scripts 11016 (escort, summons Jaedenar Legionnaires 9862 and Spirit of Trey Lightforge 11141); item 13140 Blood Red Key drops from Jaedenar warlocks, darkweavers, enforcers, legionnaires, Ulathek and Ur''dan; gameobject 176225 Arko''niran''s Chest; Rakaiah 9518 near the Remains of Trey Lightforge 11020'),
(36130, 3, 361, 3, 1, 0, 'The Jadefire Satyrs', 'Few seek adventure in Felwood, where the corruption is widespread and indiscriminate. Eridan Bluewind of the Emerald Circle means to heal the land, but some wish it to fester, and chief among them are the Jadefire satyrs at the Ruins of Constellas, northwest of the Sanctuary. Led by a particularly cruel satyr named Xavathras, with felsworn, shadowstalkers and rogues at his command, they spread their disease to every creature they meet. Eridan means to defend a land that was once her people''s, and the first blow must fall on Xavathras and his minions.', 'quests 4421, 4906 descriptions and reward texts'),
(36131, 3, 361, 4, 1, 0, 'The Flute of Xavaric', 'Among the spoils of Xavaric, master of the Jadefire satyrs in northern Felwood, is a simple wooden flute. Its knotted wood feels solid, yet the spirals and patterns on its surface seem to spin and move as it is turned in the hand, and whoever holds it is seized by a sudden dread. Perhaps the mind is only playing tricks. Other satyrs may carry clues to what it is, and the felbind they bear seems worth gathering, so the flute is taken south to the druid Eridan Bluewind of the Emerald Sanctuary.', 'quests 939, 4441, 4442 descriptions and reward texts; creature_text 9116 (Eridan''s purification lines); event_scripts 3839 (Arei summoned in Irontree Woods)'),
(36132, 3, 361, 5, 0, 0, 'Cleansing Felwood', 'Two druids of the Emerald Circle, the night elf Arathandris Silversky southeast of the Emerald Sanctuary and the tauren Maybess Riverbreeze to its west, know how to cleanse the forest''s sick plants, but they guard that knowledge closely, for in the wrong hands it would spell disaster for all of Felwood. Plants give life to the forest, and even they suffer the taint. Trust must be won first in the Irontree Cavern to the north, where warpwood elementals lost beyond any hope of cleansing are slain for the sap called blood amber, which the druids study in the hope of saving other life.', 'quests 4101, 4102 texts; quest 4103 completion and reward (beacon, soul shards, salve); npc_text 2844, 2845, 2842, 2843, 2848 (Arathandris and Maybess); creature_text 9528, 9529 (beacon); quests 996, 2523, 4117, 4119 texts (corrupted windblossom, songflower, whipper root, night dragon); creature positions: Arathandris 3805,-1472 (Morlos''Aran, southeast of the Sanctuary), Maybess 3947,-1046 (west of it)'),
(36133, 3, 361, 6, 0, 0, 'Timbermaw Ally', 'Grazle of the Timbermaw knows that outsiders kill furbolgs without asking whether they are friend or foe, so his tribe, the only one of its race to escape the corruption, trusts very few. To earn a place among its allies one must drive back the corrupted Deadwood, starting with the warriors, pathfinders and gardeners of the village southwest of the Sanctuary. At the far end of the road, Nafien, who guards the gate of Timbermaw Hold, asks the same of the Deadwood camp to his southwest, though he begs to be spared the details: the Deadwood are not evil by nature, only poisoned by the fel, and it grieves him to fight his own brethren.', 'quests 8460, 8462, 8461 descriptions and reward texts; quests 8466, 8467 (feathers); quest 8470 (Deadwood Ritual Totem to Kernda); quest 8465 reward (Winterfall under the same corruptive sway); npc_text 8123 (Nafien)');
INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_part` (`Entry`, `Part`, `MinState`, `MaxState`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(36102, 1, 0, 255, 'Word from Shatter Scar Vale ends Taronn''s hopes. The craters there still hold the corrupt, fetid water that gathered in them years ago, and his search for even one pure source in Felwood has failed. Healing the land would have been far easier with it, so now he means to save what forest creatures he can and destroy those grown too corrupt to spare.', 'quest 5156 reward text'),
(36104, 1, 0, 255, 'The well serves a larger plan. Xavathras and his minions have been cultivating the corrupted moonwell so that its spoils can be passed north to another satyr, Xavaric, master of the Jadefire encampment at Jadefire Run.', 'quest 4906 description (offered on the 4421 turn-in)'),
(36109, 1, 0, 255, 'Greta Mosshoof''s scrying, won when the four braziers were doused, names the head of the serpent. Shadow Lord Fel''dan is the mortal in power below, the one making pacts with the Burning Legion, and the straight path down through the Hold is the only way to reach him.', 'quest 5242 description'),
(36112, 1, 0, 255, 'Xavaric is more than one satyr chief among many. The Jadefire at the Ruins of Constellas were only part of a larger plan, cultivating the corrupted moonwell there so that its spoils could be delivered to him here.', 'quest 4906 description'),
(36112, 2, 0, 255, 'Xavaric''s simple wooden flute is far from simple. It was carved from an ancient protector, one of the treants that long guarded the night elves, and through fel magic the tortured spirit of that ancient remains bound within it, never released.', 'quest 939 reward text; quest 4441 description'),
(36119, 1, 0, 255, 'Even with Xavathras slain, Eridan is not at ease. She senses something much larger than the satyrs at work in Felwood, and warns that ridding the forest of one cruel satyr is only the first step in a long labor of repair.', 'quest 4421 reward text'),
(36119, 2, 0, 255, 'She is sensitive to more than satyrs. Holding the flute taken from Xavaric is almost unbearable to her, for in it she feels the suffering of ancient ones: a protector''s spirit, bound and tortured by fel magic and never released.', 'quest 939 reward text; quest 4441 description'),
(36119, 3, 0, 255, 'With blessed water from the Temple of the Moon and a prayer that Elune guide her hands and heart, Eridan banishes the evil aura from the flute and breaks the link between it and the ancient spirit bound within.', 'quest 4442 description and reward text; creature_text 9116 (on 4442 taken)'),
(36120, 1, 0, 255, 'Those who come cloaked in the Shadow Council''s own brand of evil may speak with him, for he is the dreadlord of Jaedenar, the cult''s seat. His patience, he says, spans the millennia, yet he grants a mortal no more than an instant of it. Favor is earned in blood: his groveling servant Ulathek is a spy for his rival, Lord Hel''nurath of Xoroth, who means to usurp his power, and Banehollow wants the traitor''s heart.', 'quest 7623 description and reward text; quest 7624 description'),
(36120, 2, 0, 255, 'The heart pleases him. After a week of rotting, he says, it will make a succulent treat, and perhaps he will send for Ulathek''s head to set before him as he eats. His patience grows, marginally. To one who would open a portal to Xoroth, Hel''nurath''s domain and home of the famed dreadsteeds, he allows a store of Xorothian stardust from Ur''dan, if the price is paid.', 'quest 7624 completion and reward text; quest 7625 description'),
(36121, 1, 0, 255, 'Once the core is his, Niby orders everyone to stand well back, for his greatest conjuration needs a wide berth. He bids the world bow down before his infernal destroyer, and from the sky falls a chicken. Impsy rolls on the floor laughing and tells his master he is an idiot. Niby silences his servant, undaunted: vengeance will be his, and Stormwind will meet death by chicken.', 'smart_scripts 1446900 (run on 7603 rewarded: Niby groups 0, 1, 2 and Impsy groups 0, 1); creature_text 14469 groups 0-2, 14470 groups 0-1; quest 7603 reward text'),
(36122, 1, 0, 255, 'With the key in her hands, she tells her story. She and her longtime friend Trey Lightforge came to Jaedenar to investigate the Shadow Council, but the cult caught them unprepared, took all their equipment and dragged Trey deeper into the Hold. She can still hear his screams from below, inhuman, and swears the cultists will pay. She will not leave without his sword, Lightforge, and she must warn her superiors.', 'npc_text 4113; quest 5203 description'),
(36122, 2, 0, 255, 'Arko''narin wins her way out, though the escape costs her the sight of Trey''s tormented spirit turned against her. She carries Lightforge on to Darnassus, too urgent even to stop for the druids'' healing. She does not show it, but her friend Jessir Moonbow knows that losing one of her closest friends, a Knight of the Silver Hand, is tearing her up inside.', 'quest 5203 reward text; smart_scripts 11016 (Spirit of Trey Lightforge 11141 summoned)'),
(36123, 1, 0, 255, 'The way out is hard. Maddened creatures fall upon the spirit, and Arei grieves that it must fight its own kind, urging that the fel touched beasts be put out of their misery. As Ashenvale draws near, Arei''s form changes: the true strength of its spirit returns and the cursed grasp of the forest leaves it, and at last it is at peace. Kayneth, hearing of it, holds that Felwood may one day be reclaimed, for every kind deed helps.', 'creature_text 9598 groups 1-7; npc_text 2809; quest 4261 reward text'),
(36125, 1, 0, 255, 'That task is the root of all evil for the Winterfall. Thanks to the tribe''s friends, the Timbermaw have found a way to draw out the demon that dominates their corrupted kin: a torch planted at the mouth of High Chief Winterfall''s cave will force it to show itself, and only the essence of the fallen demon can begin the Winterfall''s long healing, and the salvation of Timbermaw Hold.', 'quest 8481 description'),
(36125, 2, 0, 255, 'When the essence of the demon Xandivious is brought to him, Gorn''s gruffness gives way. The safety of Timbermaw Hold is assured for years to come, he declares, and its slayer is a hero among the furbolgs. The healing will be slow and the conflict will go on, but the Winterfall have something they never had before: a chance at survival.', 'quest 8481 reward text'),
(36125, 3, 0, 255, 'Gorn then looks beyond his own kind. Deeds such as these go beyond the tale of a simple hero, he says, and if the hero speaks for a people, the Timbermaw would make peace with them. He sends an offering of peace to the leader of the hero''s people, who in times past tried to make contact with his tribe.', 'quests 8484, 8485 descriptions'),
(36125, 4, 0, 255, 'The offering is received as a most fortuitous turn of events. A lasting peace with the Timbermaw would give the hero''s people a real advantage in Kalimdor, and word of it goes out at once to the other leaders, with more diplomats to follow.', 'quests 8484, 8485 reward texts (Magni Bronzebeard, Thrall)'),
(36126, 1, 0, 255, 'When Ror''s claw is brought to her, Dreka''Sur counts it an honor kept. Her husband died in battle, she says, and he would have been proud of that, but she could not rest until the creature that left her to live her life alone had paid for what it had done.', 'quest 6162 reward text'),
(36127, 1, 0, 255, 'The sample works as she hoped. A little of the water made her kitten double in size and grow stronger, somehow, and Winna wants the cat carried to the moonwell itself and released there, promising with a chuckle that the results will please. Such cats, she thinks, may prove useful.', 'quest 4506 description'),
(36127, 2, 0, 255, 'What comes back from the moonwell is no kitten but a corrupted saber, following its keeper obediently. Winna is delighted: the Forsaken, she says, will resort to any means necessary to crush the Alliance, and the corrupted water will surely prove useful in their future efforts.', 'quest 4506 reward text; creature_template 10042 Corrupted Saber, creature_text 10042 (follows obediently); spell 15647, smart_scripts 9937 and actionlist 993700 (kitten turned into 10042 at the moonwell)'),
(36128, 1, 0, 255, 'With the cult''s numbers thinned, Greta reveals her plan. Shadow Hold, the fortress deep within Jaedenar, is guarded by protective spells bound to braziers, and while they burn her scrying cannot reach inside to learn who leads the Council. Purified water could douse them, so a canteen is carried to the Moon Well at the center of Jaedenar and filled with its corrupt water.', 'quest 5155 reward text; quest 5157 description and completion text'),
(36128, 2, 0, 255, 'Purifying it will take travel. Greta sends the water to the Barrens, to a small camp on the shore south of Ratchet, where her old friend, the shaman Islen Waterseer, keeps a strong bond with the spirits of water. A cause so noble, Greta trusts, should persuade both Islen and the spirits to help.', 'quest 5157 reward text; quest 5158 description'),
(36128, 3, 0, 255, 'The spirits judge the cause just, and Islen sends the purified water back with her regards and a warning: the Shadow Council is not a force to be trifled with, and Greta is tackling something greater than many know. Greta takes heart from the blessing, and the water is carried into Shadow Hold to douse the four braziers of protection.', 'quest 5159 description and reward text; quest 5165 description'),
(36128, 4, 0, 255, 'As the last brazier''s flame dies, Greta''s spells pierce the Hold, and before the Council''s warlocks can restore their wards she learns enough, she hopes, to strike. Going into a dragon''s lair without knowledge is a fool''s errand, she says, and the Shadow Council is far worse than any dragon.', 'quest 5165 completion and reward text'),
(36128, 5, 0, 255, 'What she learned points to one man. There is no other way into Shadow Hold than the straight path down, and at its bottom waits Shadow Lord Fel''dan, the mortal in power below, the head of the serpent and the one making pacts with the Legion. He and his two succubus servants must die.', 'quest 5242 description'),
(36128, 6, 0, 255, 'Fel''dan falls with his succubi, Moora and Salia, and his head is carried back to the Emerald Sanctuary. Greta praises the Earthmother: with such a blow to its hierarchy the Council will be hard pressed to regain its old power, and without Fel''dan she hopes it will lose focus and turn to infighting, the moment to strike its demons hardest.', 'quest 5242 completion and reward text'),
(36129, 1, 0, 255, 'The key fits a cage within Shadow Hold, and in it is the night elf Arko''narin, one of Jessir''s missing friends. Even once the cage is open she will not simply flee: first she must recover the sword Lightforge, which belonged to her companion Trey, along with her own gear, and escape the Hold to warn her superiors of what is happening there.', 'quest 5202 completion and reward text; quest 5203 description'),
(36129, 2, 0, 255, 'The escape is hard won. Arko''narin finds her gear among candles laid out for some dark ritual and fights her way out past the cult''s legionnaires, and then Trey himself appears, his tormented spirit turned against her. She hurries on to Darnassus with Lightforge, and Jessir, knowing how the loss of this Knight of the Silver Hand will haunt her friend, asks for his torturer, the succubus Rakaiah, to be slain and his remains found.', 'smart_scripts 11016 and creature_text 11016, 11141; quest 5203 reward text; quest 5204 description and log'),
(36129, 3, 0, 255, 'Rakaiah is slain, and near her lie the remains of Trey Lightforge, beyond doubt the Knight of the Silver Hand who came into Jaedenar with Arko''narin. They are gathered with care, and there is comfort in knowing that at least his spirit has been released from the pain forced upon it.', 'quest 5204 completion and reward text; quest 5385 description'),
(36129, 4, 0, 255, 'Carried back to Jessir on the border of Felwood and Ashenvale, the remains can at last be given proper respect. Jessir gives thanks to Elune, certain that Arko''narin will be glad her rescuer not only saved her but also slew the creature who tortured one of her best friends.', 'quest 5385 description and reward text'),
(36130, 1, 0, 255, 'Xavathras''s death is only the first step in a long process of repair, and Eridan senses something larger than the satyrs at work. Part of the truth soon follows: Xavathras and his minions served a larger plan, cultivating the corrupted moonwell at Constellas to provide its spoils to Xavaric, whose camp lies to the north, where hellcallers and tricksters feed upon the corruption of the forest''s native creatures.', 'quest 4421 reward text; quest 4906 description'),
(36130, 2, 0, 255, 'In the north Xavaric falls among his hellcallers and tricksters, and his camp''s torment of Felwood''s creatures is ended. Eridan gives thanks and asks that Elune protect and guide her champion on the path ahead, knowing that the long labor of healing the forest has only begun.', 'quest 4906 completion and reward text; quest 4421 reward text'),
(36131, 1, 0, 255, 'Eridan can hardly bear to hold it. She senses the suffering of ancient ones: the flute was carved from an ancient protector, one of the treants that long guarded the night elves, and through fel magic the satyrs have bound its spirit to suffer without release. The felbind is surely part of it. To purify the flute she needs blessed water from the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus.', 'quest 939 reward text; quest 4441 description'),
(36131, 2, 0, 255, 'The blessed water is brought from Darnassus, and Eridan prays that it will release the ancient''s spirit and let it rest. With the water of Elune she begins the purification, asking that Elune guide her hands and heart.', 'quest 4441 completion and reward text; quest 4442 description; creature_text 9116'),
(36131, 3, 0, 255, 'As she prays, Eridan feels the presence of evil leaving the flute, and the link between flute and spirit is broken. She believes the flute may now summon the spirits of ancients if played in a sacred place, perhaps the ruins in the southern part of Irontree Woods, where many corrupted treants once lived and where they may linger still, even in spirit form.', 'quest 4442 reward text; creature_text 9116 groups 0, 1 (smart_scripts 911600, run on 4442 taken)'),
(36131, 4, 0, 255, 'Played among those ruins, the flute brings forth Arei, the spirit of an ancient protector still trapped by Felwood''s corruption, who begs to be led out of the cursed forest so that it may finally rest.', 'event_scripts 3839 (Arei summoned in 1767); quest 4261 description; creature_text 9598 group 0'),
(36132, 1, 0, 255, 'With the blood amber delivered, trust is given. It may seem odd that killing the elementals proved anything, the druid admits, but saving countless lives must justify the means. Then the craft is shared. A Cenarion beacon lets its bearer see the corruption the naked eye misses, and the corrupted soul shards that tainted beasts leave behind, and from such shards the druids grind the reagent for Cenarion plant salve.', 'quests 4101, 4102 reward text; npc_text 2848, 2849 (beacon); creature_text 9528, 9529; quests 4103, 5882 completion text (soul shards, salve)'),
(36132, 2, 0, 255, 'Spread on one of Felwood''s sick plants, whether songflower, windblossom, night dragon or slime coated whipper root, the Cenarion plant salve works at once. The plant sheds its corrupted form and blossoms vibrant and healthy again, one small patch of the old forest given back its life.', 'quests 996, 2523, 4117, 4119 completion and reward texts; gameobject_queststarter: 29 Corrupted Songflower, Windblossom, Whipper Root and Night Dragon quests, QuestSortID 361, QuestType 0'),
(36133, 1, 0, 255, 'Grazle takes the help as a sign of growing friendship, for the Timbermaw suffer much from the events of the past, and he sends the proven north along the road to Nafien. The guard may look a feral and unsavory beast, Grazle warns, but he is not to be feared: he only seeks aid against the malign forces that threaten their home.', 'quest 8460 reward text; quest 8462 description'),
(36133, 2, 0, 255, 'Nafien has heard word on the wind of outsiders seeking the Timbermaw''s friendship, and he welcomes them, but warns that his tribe reacts poorly to strangers. In these trying times they trust only those who fight the corruption alongside them and prove it, and any who have not will be met with open hostility within the Hold.', 'quest 8462 reward text'),
(36133, 3, 0, 255, 'When the camp is broken, Nafien senses the victory without needing to hear of it. Victory, he says, is a hollow word for what had to be done. Still, the deed proves its doer worthy, and though it may take time before the Timbermaw welcome them without hostility, perseverance will wear down suspicion, so long as no weapon is ever raised against the tribe.', 'quest 8461 reward text'),
(36133, 4, 0, 255, 'Trust grows slowly. The suspicious brethren of the tribe still need convincing, and the distinctive headdresses some Deadwood wear give proof of every blow struck against them: each set of feathers brought in makes the bearer''s deeds known among the Timbermaw.', 'quests 8466, 8467 completion and reward text'),
(36133, 5, 0, 255, 'Inside the Hold, Kernda takes a Deadwood ritual totem thick with the stench of decay. Whatever foulness has turned the Deadwood against their kin, Kernda says, is surely present in it, and through study and ritual the Timbermaw hope to uncover what pollutes the minds of their brethren.', 'quest 8470 reward text');
